{"3099620": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "Fablelight", "steam_appid": 3099620, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "controller_support": "full", "dlc": [5043460], "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3099620/extras/51b5f4ff1c908bd91e2a3446b35b19be.avif?t=1788207416\" width=1560 height=340 /></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Traditional Fighting Game Combat, Built for Single-Player</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >What if there was a traditional <u><strong>JRPG</strong></u> with a battle system that plays like a <u><strong>fighting game</strong></u>? What if a fighting game took single-player content seriously? <br><br>Fablelight blends <strong>tight, traditional fighting game mechanics</strong> with a fully playable story campaign focusing on single-player content first, instead of online ranked.</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >fight one-on-one battles</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >progress through a branching route</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >earn experience &amp; level up</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >unlock skills &amp; abilities</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >recruit new allies, discover playable characters</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >shape your story with alternate paths</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3099620/extras/fdbacfad590890222b28449fe43e0608.poster.avif?t=1788207416\" width=794 height=334 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3099620/extras/fdbacfad590890222b28449fe43e0608.webm?t=1788207416\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3099620/extras/fdbacfad590890222b28449fe43e0608.mp4?t=1788207416\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Battle through a handcrafted world as <strong>Rojas</strong>, a glass canon fighter wielding a magical sword with cosmic power, and uncover a twisted fairytale filled with secrets, allies, and branching paths. Learn mid-range zoning from <strong>Granny Boom,</strong> the crazed pyromaniac and demolition expert, or simply button mash the <i>unga bunga</i> barbarian <strong>Krog.</strong> There's a character for every playstyle.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3099620/extras/193e66a0bb4359c0ed6b33e82079657d.avif?t=1788207416\" width=1560 height=340 /></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Motion Inputs, Special Cancels, Cross-Ups</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you play fighting games, <i>this will feel familiar</i>. If you don’t, the game teaches you through gameplay -- not tutorials that stop the action.<br><br>Combat in <i>Fablelight</i> is built on <strong>traditional fighting-game fundamentals</strong>:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Hold back to block</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Motion inputs</strong> (quarter-circles, charge, 360 motions)</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>One-on-one 2D battles</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Hand-drawn sprite animation</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Precise hitboxes, spacing, and timing</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\"><strong></strong><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3099620/extras/c4206e6d1a31bd110e86cfe620157e50.poster.avif?t=1788207416\" width=794 height=334 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3099620/extras/c4206e6d1a31bd110e86cfe620157e50.webm?t=1788207416\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3099620/extras/c4206e6d1a31bd110e86cfe620157e50.mp4?t=1788207416\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span>Traditional fighting game archetypes: Grapplers, Zoners, Rush-Down  <br>+  <br>JRPG Archetypes: Black Mage, Healers, Warriors  </p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3099620/extras/6e520228ba3d678f341336a14a27a4c1.avif?t=1788207416\" width=1560 height=340 /></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Skill Tree for Each Character, Job System Inspired by FFT</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Outside of battle, <i>Fablelight</i> expands into a full <strong>action RPG structure</strong>:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Character leveling and skill trees</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Unlockable abilities and combat mechanics</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Equipment and gear that meaningfully affect play</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Exploration across a connected world map</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Branching paths, optional encounters, and secrets</strong></p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" style=\"text-align: center\">Progression enhances your options, but <strong>skill always matters</strong>!<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3099620/extras/638213cbfdbe5e6ccfdf0e377ac0d7db.poster.avif?t=1788207416\" width=794 height=334 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3099620/extras/638213cbfdbe5e6ccfdf0e377ac0d7db.webm?t=1788207416\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3099620/extras/638213cbfdbe5e6ccfdf0e377ac0d7db.mp4?t=1788207416\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3099620/extras/80b6ba5fe0eaa7ce9e65cfd349ebdb48.avif?t=1788207416\" width=1560 height=340 /></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Fully Fleshed Out Worlds</strong> with <strong>Multiple Hidden Paths</strong> &amp; Characters to Discover</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Set in a strange, fairy-tale-inspired world, <i>Fablelight</i> tells a <strong>character-driven original story</strong> through battles, dialogue, and player choice without relying on long cinematic cutscenes.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>", "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3099620/extras/51b5f4ff1c908bd91e2a3446b35b19be.avif?t=1788207416\" width=1560 height=340 /></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Traditional Fighting Game Combat, Built for Single-Player</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >What if there was a traditional <u><strong>JRPG</strong></u> with a battle system that plays like a <u><strong>fighting game</strong></u>? What if a fighting game took single-player content seriously? <br><br>Fablelight blends <strong>tight, traditional fighting game mechanics</strong> with a fully playable story campaign focusing on single-player content first, instead of online ranked.</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >fight one-on-one battles</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >progress through a branching route</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >earn experience &amp; level up</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >unlock skills &amp; abilities</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >recruit new allies, discover playable characters</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >shape your story with alternate paths</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3099620/extras/fdbacfad590890222b28449fe43e0608.poster.avif?t=1788207416\" width=794 height=334 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3099620/extras/fdbacfad590890222b28449fe43e0608.webm?t=1788207416\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3099620/extras/fdbacfad590890222b28449fe43e0608.mp4?t=1788207416\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Battle through a handcrafted world as <strong>Rojas</strong>, a glass canon fighter wielding a magical sword with cosmic power, and uncover a twisted fairytale filled with secrets, allies, and branching paths. Learn mid-range zoning from <strong>Granny Boom,</strong> the crazed pyromaniac and demolition expert, or simply button mash the <i>unga bunga</i> barbarian <strong>Krog.</strong> There's a character for every playstyle.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3099620/extras/193e66a0bb4359c0ed6b33e82079657d.avif?t=1788207416\" width=1560 height=340 /></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Motion Inputs, Special Cancels, Cross-Ups</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you play fighting games, <i>this will feel familiar</i>. If you don’t, the game teaches you through gameplay -- not tutorials that stop the action.<br><br>Combat in <i>Fablelight</i> is built on <strong>traditional fighting-game fundamentals</strong>:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Hold back to block</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Motion inputs</strong> (quarter-circles, charge, 360 motions)</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>One-on-one 2D battles</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Hand-drawn sprite animation</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Precise hitboxes, spacing, and timing</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\"><strong></strong><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3099620/extras/c4206e6d1a31bd110e86cfe620157e50.poster.avif?t=1788207416\" width=794 height=334 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3099620/extras/c4206e6d1a31bd110e86cfe620157e50.webm?t=1788207416\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3099620/extras/c4206e6d1a31bd110e86cfe620157e50.mp4?t=1788207416\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span>Traditional fighting game archetypes: Grapplers, Zoners, Rush-Down  <br>+  <br>JRPG Archetypes: Black Mage, Healers, Warriors  </p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3099620/extras/6e520228ba3d678f341336a14a27a4c1.avif?t=1788207416\" width=1560 height=340 /></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Skill Tree for Each Character, Job System Inspired by FFT</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Outside of battle, <i>Fablelight</i> expands into a full <strong>action RPG structure</strong>:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Character leveling and skill trees</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Unlockable abilities and combat mechanics</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Equipment and gear that meaningfully affect play</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Exploration across a 